Psalm 119:9-16

9 How shall a yóuth remáin púre on his wáy?
By obéying your wórd.
10 I have sóught you with áll my héart;
let me not stráy from your commánds.

11 I tréasure your wórd in my héart,
lest I sín agáinst you.
12 Blést are yóu, O LÓRD;
téach me your státutes.

13 With my líps have I recóunted
all the decrées of your móuth.
14 I rejóice in the wáy of your précepts,
as though all ríches were míne.

15 I will pónder your précepts,
and consíder your páths.
16 I take delíght in your státutes;
I will not forgét your wórd.

Glóry to the Fáther, and to the Són,
and to the Hóly Spírit:
as it wás in the begínning, is nów,
and will be for éver. Amén.
